Metadata (titles, dates, numbers, links) taken from WIPO Lex, https://www.wipo.int/wipolex/, retrieved 30 October 2026. Source: World Intellectual Property Organization. WIPO content is published under CC BY 4.0 (https://www.wipo.int/web/terms-of-use); only facts are copied, with no descriptive text. Open facts about the legal system come from Wikidata, https://www.wikidata.org/ (CC0 1.0).

No law text is included: no law text, because the official online copies of Burundi's Constitution and statutes (presidence.gov.bi, assemblee.bi) are image scans with no text layer, OCR was not available here, and no text-layer official copy was found. The copyright act (Loi n° 1/021 of 30 December 2005) is itself only a scan on assemblee.bi, so whether it excludes official texts could not be checked, and no third-party copy of a law is used.

Catalogue entries for the laws of 2003-2012 record only facts (law number, promulgation date, link) taken from the file names in the public media index of the Assemblée nationale du Burundi, https://assemblee.bi/, retrieved 30 October 2026. No text of any law is copied.

Treaty actions (treaty name, action, date, depositary) come from the UN Treaty Collection, https://treaties.un.org/, as facts only; no treaty text is copied.

Changes made by Lexifina: records were turned into one Markdown file per record, with the dates arranged as a git history. WIPO does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the
tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
